<resources>
    <!-- The LED pattern held while the TV is on, until the owner picks another on the card screen (Left/Right)
         or over ADB, by starting io.github.mattaltus.speakerleds/.LedActivity with the string extra "pattern" (see README).
         One of: listening, thinking, responding, timeout, mute, error. On a TCL 43C725 "mute" is a steady
         light that matches the stock look; "listening" is a steady light too. -->
    <string name="led_pattern" translatable="false">mute</string>
    <!-- Light the LEDs only while TCL's far-field mic is off, and keep them dark while it is on, as Google's voice
         app (katniss) did on stock firmware. The mic state is content://atv.hotwordmic/togglestate (TCL's
         com.tcl.system.server); a TV without it keeps the pattern on. false: always on, a power light. -->
    <bool name="follow_mic">true</bool>
</resources>
